Z||000003||brharris27370||12-18-2001||04:35 PM||||Is there an external way to tell the rear gear on a trans that is not in the car.  Did only the 84's get the 4.10 gear.||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPAW||12-19-2001||09:37 AM||||Behind the four cylinder engine the 4.10 gearing does o.k. - accelerates good and high crusing rpm is hardly noticeable but the acceleration was not noticably stronger than the isuzu 5spds I have driven (in Fieros with stock, high milage engines)<P>Behind a high torque engine like a SBC the 4.10 gearing makes first gear almost completely useless unless your engine runs strong up to 6000-6500 RPM.  I also found the high cruise RPMs to be unbearable. Because of this I am in the process of switching to a 5spd on my v8 Fiero.<P>I would think on a v6 you could see some serious improvement on zero to 60 times with the 4.10 gearing if your engine is built to run to the higher RPMs. Maybe someone else has some experience with this setup?<P>Paul<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||GT Bastard||12-19-2001||02:45 PM||||Definitely go 4.10 Rich...  Especially since you've got the Acura for highway trips. 1st gear clutch dumps launch the car like a space shuttle.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/icare.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||MooCow||12-19-2001||03:12 PM||||I have the 4:10 in my 3.4 and I dont do a lot of highway driving and I get about 22 MPG.  Also my car is a 3.4.  I was going to get the Isuzu with my 4:10 but after talking to Ed Parks about it, I stuck with the 4:10 cause of the low end.  I wouldn't say that highway driving is annoying cause I am only at 3,200 RPMS on th highway.  Also on the highway I can just touch the gas and man it goes real nice.  Only bad thing is that I can't go any faster than 105 MPH cause I hit redline in the car, but I never drive that fast.  If you like stop light to stop light racing or accelerating then go with the 4:10.<BR>Also the 4:10 came only in 84 Fiero's and also in 84 they had another tranny but I think thos were only in some base coupes.  If you have any more questions on the 4:10 let me know.  Truthfully I am happy that I didn't switch mine to a 5-speed.<P>Thanks Ken<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forum_pic.jpg">  <BR>AOL=MooCow888||||reg||10
